values ('c4a8e2d7-1b59-4f06-9a31-6d0e5c3b8f18', 'health-economics', 'Health Economics', 'This course provides an advanced economic analysis of health systems, covering fundamental topics such as the demand for health, healthcare supply, insurance markets, and cost-effectiveness. Students will explore healthcare financing, international comparisons, and value-based care through the lens of public health equity. The curriculum emphasizes practical applications, including budget impact analysis, prevention effectiveness, causal policy evaluation, and global financing strategies, culminating in an applied economic decision memo.');

